# Character classification

Classify and case-fold ASCII code points (as Int), the char-level counterpart of the string
predicates. Pure LOGOS, identical on every tier. Auto-imported on reference.

## Note
True when `c` is an ASCII decimal digit (codepoints 48 to 57, `0`-`9`).

## To charIsDigit (c: Int) -> Bool:
    If c is less than 48:
        Return false.
    If c is greater than 57:
        Return false.
    Return true.

## Note
True when `c` is an ASCII uppercase letter (codepoints 65 to 90, `A`-`Z`).

## To charIsUpper (c: Int) -> Bool:
    If c is less than 65:
        Return false.
    If c is greater than 90:
        Return false.
    Return true.

## Note
True when `c` is an ASCII lowercase letter (codepoints 97 to 122, `a`-`z`).

## To charIsLower (c: Int) -> Bool:
    If c is less than 97:
        Return false.
    If c is greater than 122:
        Return false.
    Return true.

## Note
True when `c` is an ASCII letter, that is uppercase or lowercase.

## To charIsLetter (c: Int) -> Bool:
    If charIsUpper(c):
        Return true.
    If charIsLower(c):
        Return true.
    Return false.

## Note
True when `c` is an ASCII letter or digit.

## To charIsAlnum (c: Int) -> Bool:
    If charIsLetter(c):
        Return true.
    If charIsDigit(c):
        Return true.
    Return false.

## Note
True for ASCII whitespace: space (32), tab (9), newline (10), carriage return (13), vertical tab (11), and form feed (12).

## To charIsSpace (c: Int) -> Bool:
    If c is equal to 32:
        Return true.
    If c is equal to 9:
        Return true.
    If c is equal to 10:
        Return true.
    If c is equal to 13:
        Return true.
    If c is equal to 11:
        Return true.
    If c is equal to 12:
        Return true.
    Return false.

## Note
True when `c` is a hexadecimal digit: `0`-`9`, `A`-`F` (65-70), or `a`-`f` (97-102).

## To charIsHexDigit (c: Int) -> Bool:
    If charIsDigit(c):
        Return true.
    If c is at least 65:
        If c is at most 70:
            Return true.
    If c is at least 97:
        If c is at most 102:
            Return true.
    Return false.

## Note
True for ASCII punctuation in the ranges 33-47, 58-64, 91-96, and 123-126.

## To charIsPunct (c: Int) -> Bool:
    If c is at least 33:
        If c is at most 47:
            Return true.
    If c is at least 58:
        If c is at most 64:
            Return true.
    If c is at least 91:
        If c is at most 96:
            Return true.
    If c is at least 123:
        If c is at most 126:
            Return true.
    Return false.

## Note
Uppercases an ASCII lowercase letter by subtracting 32; other codepoints are returned unchanged.

## To charToUpper (c: Int) -> Int:
    If charIsLower(c):
        Return c - 32.
    Return c.

## Note
Lowercases an ASCII uppercase letter by adding 32; other codepoints are returned unchanged.

## To charToLower (c: Int) -> Int:
    If charIsUpper(c):
        Return c + 32.
    Return c.

## Note
True for ASCII control characters: codepoints below 32 or the DEL character (127).

## To charIsControl (c: Int) -> Bool:
    If c is less than 32:
        Return true.
    If c is equal to 127:
        Return true.
    Return false.

## Note
True for printable ASCII, codepoints 32 to 126 inclusive (space through `~`).

## To charIsPrint (c: Int) -> Bool:
    If c is at least 32:
        If c is at most 126:
            Return true.
    Return false.

## Note
True only for the two ASCII blank characters: space (32) and tab (9).

## To charIsBlank (c: Int) -> Bool:
    If c is equal to 32:
        Return true.
    If c is equal to 9:
        Return true.
    Return false.

## Note
True for visible ASCII graphic characters, codepoints 33 to 126 (printable but not space).

## To charIsGraph (c: Int) -> Bool:
    If c is at least 33:
        If c is at most 126:
            Return true.
    Return false.

## Note
Titlecases a character by uppercasing an ASCII lowercase letter (subtracting 32); other codepoints are returned unchanged.

## To charToTitle (c: Int) -> Int:
    If c is at least 97:
        If c is at most 122:
            Return c - 32.
    Return c.

## Note
True when `c` is a titlecase character, that is an ASCII uppercase letter (codepoints 65 to 90).

## To charIsTitle (c: Int) -> Bool:
    If c is at least 65:
        If c is at most 90:
            Return true.
    Return false.

## Note
The numeric value 0-9 of an ASCII digit, or -1 when `c` is not a digit.

## To charDigitVal (c: Int) -> Int:
    If c is at least 48:
        If c is at most 57:
            Return c - 48.
    Return 0 - 1.
